# Review: StreamDeckPlugin

The plugin meets almost all of its spec, and the pure parts are well tested. The model lives in
`plugin-space`'s `Dashboard` module. `toShortcuts`, `findFavoriteTag`, `toMetrics` and
`toSpaceStats` have tests for the favorite tag, label sort, keyed-tag rejection, task takeover,
indeterminate progress and stats fallback. The renderer (`renderKey`, `renderDial`, `buildFrame`,
`wrapText`, `escapeXml`) and `StreamDeckBridge` also have tests, which cover backoff, frame dedup and
the incompatible stop. The device side (`packages/apps/composer-stream-deck`) tests its server and
slot ordering.

The gaps are in the glue. `bridge-driver.ts`, the module that owns the single bridge, maps presses to
`LayoutOperation.Open` and brings the window forward, has no test. Neither do the three React
components. So F-1.5, F-4.5, F-4.6 and the press half of T-5 are untested. F-3.4 is close but not
literal: the panel and the driver each call `buildFrame` from their own queries (`useFavorites` and
`SpaceCapabilities.Dashboard`), so they share code but not one frame object. Both QA tests are manual.

